{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**1. Contradictions**\n- #7/#4 detached supervisor + file-only truth vs `job_registry` in-process threads and RAM state — **Ruling:** real supervisor; files are SoT.\n- #4 `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/` vs `status_record.rs` `cursor-delegate-jobs` — **Ruling:** `delegate-jobs` per #4.\n- #4 RUNNING record needs supervisor pid; `PollResult::Running` has none — **Ruling:** add `supervisorPid`.\n- #4 cwd lock file across processes vs in-memory `path_lock` — **Ruling:** file lock for CLI BUSY.\n- #4 terminal record must carry resume fields (cwd, capability, gate); `RunOutput` lacks them — **Ruling:** `resume` object on disk.\n- #7 STATUS-only prompt vs `compose_prompt` preamble/verify on MCP path — **Ruling:** CLI STATUS-only; MCP unchanged.\n- #7 tracer omits `--gate`/`--tool-idle-ms` that #4 documents — **Ruling:** defer flags; core path first.\n\n**2. Unstated defaults**\n- Job id: `random_uuid()` — **Ruling:** keep UUID strings.\n- Record JSON: existing `PollResult` + extensions — **Ruling:** camelCase serde.\n- Heartbeat: `HEARTBEAT_MS` = 30s — **Ruling:** 30s unless probed.\n- `watch` stdout shape — **Ruling:** one compact JSON object per job, newline-separated.\n- `watch` exit on timeout — **Ruling:** exit 1 if any job still RUNNING.\n- Binary: only `cursor-delegate-mcp` in `Cargo.toml` — **Ruling:** add `delegate` bin on shared lib.\n- `--timeout S`: seconds vs registry ms — **Ruling:** CLI seconds; internal ms.\n\n**3. Silent failures**\n- `FileStatusRecordWriter` drops write/rename errors — **Ruling:** supervisor logs and exits non-zero.\n- Missing/unreadable status file during `watch` — **Ruling:** treat as NOT_FOUND; block until timeout.\n- Orphan RUNNING after supervisor death — **Ruling:** stale heartbeat policy (document only for #7).\n- Unknown model: allow-list message vs cursor stderr catalog (#4 probe) — **Ruling:** stderr lists all configured ids.\n- Empty stdin/`--prompt-file` — **Ruling:** validation error, exit 2.\n\n**4. Acceptance vs spec/code**\n- E2E must hit `delegate` binary; `tests/e2e.rs` drives MCP only — **Ruling:** new CLI e2e; keep MCP green.\n- “Valid ids” vs `ModelNotAllowedError` wording — **Ruling:** enumerate ids on stderr.\n- “Print once terminal” vs timeout with RUNNING jobs — **Ruling:** print last snapshot; non-zero exit.\n- Fixtures via recording script while #7 blocked on #6 — **Ruling:** land #6 fixtures before asserting streams.\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS"}]},"session_id":"36627d89-4873-4238-8376-e9782bc73a39"}
